   "title": {
    "en": "Placentation"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Placentation is the arrangement of ovules in the ovary. Marginal: the placenta forms a ridge along the ventral suture of a one-chambered ovary, as in pea. Axile: ovules are attached to a central placenta in a multi-chambered ovary, as in China rose, tomato and lemon. Parietal: ovules develop on the inner wall of the ovary, which becomes two-chambered by a false septum, as in mustard and Argemone. Free central: ovules are borne on a central axis with no septa, as in Dianthus and Primrose. Basal: a single ovule is attached at the base of the ovary, as in sunflower and marigold.",
    "kn": "ಜರಾಯು ವಿನ್ಯಾಸ: ಅಂಚಿನ (ಬಟಾಣಿ), ಅಕ್ಷೀಯ (ದಾಸವಾಳ, ಟೊಮೆಟೊ, ನಿಂಬೆ), ಭಿತ್ತಿಯ (ಸಾಸಿವೆ, ಆರ್ಜಿಮೋನ್), ಸ್ವತಂತ್ರ ಕೇಂದ್ರೀಯ (ಡಯಾಂಥಸ್, ಪ್ರಿಮ್‌ರೋಸ್), ತಳದ (ಸೂರ್ಯಕಾಂತಿ, ಚೆಂಡುಹೂ)."
